From: Playtendoh
Subject: [PATCH] HQX: its RGB to YUV table on the heap, made when the filter is first chosen

The table was 64 MiB of zeroes in the app's image (.bss) whether or not a game ever used the HQX
filter. With ParaLLEl-N64's memory added the image grew to 503 MiB, and the console restarted as
the app started, most likely as the image went over what the PS5 gives a title. hqxInit, which every HQX use calls first, now makes it.

---
diff --git a/Utilities/HQX/common.h b/Utilities/HQX/common.h
index dbd6c33..bb3bd36 100644
--- a/Utilities/HQX/common.h
+++ b/Utilities/HQX/common.h
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
 #define trV   0x00000006
 
 /* RGB to YUV lookup table */
-extern uint32_t RGBtoYUV[16777216];
+extern uint32_t* RGBtoYUV; /* PS5: hqxInit makes it */
 
 static inline uint32_t rgb_to_yuv(uint32_t c)
 {
diff --git a/Utilities/HQX/init.cpp b/Utilities/HQX/init.cpp
index be9de48..692ec29 100644
--- a/Utilities/HQX/init.cpp
+++ b/Utilities/HQX/init.cpp
@@ -20,12 +20,16 @@
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include "hqx.h"
 
-uint32_t   RGBtoYUV[16777216];
+uint32_t*  RGBtoYUV;
 uint32_t   YUV1, YUV2;
 
 void HQX_CALLCONV hqxInit(void)
 {
     /* Initalize RGB to YUV lookup table */
+    /* PS5: made here, on the heap, when the filter is first chosen: 64 MiB in the app's image (.bss)
+       counts against what the PS5 gives a title, used or not */
+    if (!RGBtoYUV)
+        RGBtoYUV = new uint32_t[16777216]();
     uint32_t c, r, g, b, y, u, v;
     for (c = 0; c < 16777215; c++) {
         r = (c & 0xFF0000) >> 16;
